-- title:
--   Non-commuting away-from-v units in a definite quaternion order
-- statement:
--   Let $\bar r$ be a prime and let $a_1, b_1$ be rationals such that the quaternion algebra $H = \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q}, a_1, b_1]$ satisfies `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a₁ b₁ rbar`, i.e. $a_1 < 0$, $b_1 < 0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the completion $H \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ has the property that every nonzero element is a unit exactly when $\bar r$ lies in the prime ideal of $v$. Let $R \subseteq H$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is an order in the sense of `IsOrder`: it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, its $\mathbb{Q}$-span is all of $H$, and it is finitely generated over $\mathbb{Z}$. Let $r$ be a prime with $r \neq \bar r$, and let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ containing the image of $r$. Write $\tilde\Gamma =$ `awayUnits R v` for the subgroup of $H^\times$ consisting of those units whose image in $(H \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_w)^\times$ lies, for every height-one prime $w \neq v$, in the subgroup generated by the local box units of $R$ at $w$ (those units $u$ for which both $u$ and $u^{-1}$ lie in the local box `localBox R w`). Then there exist $x, y \in \tilde\Gamma$ whose images in $H$ satisfy $xy \neq yx$.
--
--   The group `awayUnits R v` plays the role of the $S$-arithmetic unit group $R[1/r]^\times$ acting on the Bruhat–Tits tree at $v$ in the Čerednik–Drinfeld setting; the assertion is that this group is non-abelian, which rules out the degenerate commutative case. It feeds into [`CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.span_val_image_awayUnits_eq_top_of_isDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.span_val_image_awayUnits_eq_top_of_isDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt), where the $\mathbb{Q}$-span of the away-from-$v$ units is shown to be all of $H$.
-- source:
